From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 79/79] PC5: a game's crash handler no longer ends the game, folders
 opened by name a second way work, and the shader compiler's listings assemble
 (Wine patches 0995, 0996, 0997)

0995: a game that starts its crash handler (handler.exe, or a program
given a crash database or upload address) at launch was taken for a
launcher handing over to another program, and closed. Such a program is
a helper now: it doesn't start, and the game goes on.

0996: a folder opened relative to another one by its name, as patch 0943
does when the folder's descriptor can't be used, was refused by Wine's
server ("the path is invalid"), so .NET games on a USB drive lost
whole folders of their data. The server takes it now.

0997: the listing the shader compiler's stand-in writes gives def values
as plain numbers, which D3DXAssembleShader reads (it refused the
exponents), and a vs_1_x shader that can't be compiled for vs_1_x is
compiled for vs_2_0.
